#1404. Number of Steps to Reduce a Number in Binary Representation to One
#Leetcode Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-steps-to-reduce-a-number-in-binary-representation-to-one/description/?envType=daily-question&envId=2026-02-26

1️ We reduce the binary number to "1" using two operations:

If even → divide by 2

If odd → add 1

2️ In binary, even numbers end with 0, so dividing by 2 just means remove the last bit.

3️ Odd numbers end with 1, so adding 1 causes a carry, turning trailing 1s into 0s until a 0 becomes 1.

4️ Instead of actually modifying the string, we simulate this using a carry variable while scanning from right to left.

5️ If (bit + carry) becomes odd → it takes 2 steps (add + divide).
If it becomes even → it takes 1 step (divide only).

6️ We process each bit once, count steps, and finally add one more step if a carry remains.

Complexity

Time: O(n)

Space: O(1)

/**
 * @param {string} s
 * @return {number}
 */
var numSteps = function(s) {
    let st=0;
    let c=0;
    for(let i=s.length-1;i>0;i--){
        let x=Number(s[i]);
        if(x+c==1){
            st+=2;
            c=1;
        }else{
            st++;
        }
    }
    if(c==1)st++;
    return st;
};
